														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2366257">
									

<p>I think safe is justified. There are plenty of objects in storage that could cause trouble if they started acting in ways we couldn't anticipate, but we by definition can't anticipate those, and if we tried, every such object would be Euclid or Keter. The Foundation <em>has</em> to work at least partially on the assumption that previous patterns hold, otherwise containment wouldn't make sense because any object could possibly do anything at any time.</p>

